Title: WIZARD IN THE ENGINE ROOM
Credit: Final Draft Screenplay (Draft 2)
Author: SNL Writers Room
Draft date: 2026-02-03
Contact:
    SNL Sketch
    Runtime: 3.5 minutes

===

FADE IN:

INT. USS ENTERPRISE - ENGINE ROOM - DAY

The engine room looks like a typical Star Trek set, but with mystical additions: floating candles, a cauldron bubbling in the corner, and constellation charts mixed with star maps. WIZARD CLIF HIGH (mid-70s, magnificent long white beard, slightly stooped but spry, Starfleet robes with wizard hat, carrying an ornate staff) stands at the center, waving his staff dramatically.

CAPTAIN (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Clif, we need warp 9 to Rigel VII. Make it so.

Clif pauses, sighs deeply.

CLIF
(muttering, rolling his eyes)
"Make it so." Like I'm some kind of vending machine. You'd think after 200 years they'd figure out warp drive on their own, but nooo... physics says it's impossible, so they need wizards.
(raises staff, speaks clearly)
Velocitas Maxima Stellarum!

The ship LURCHES forward. Magical sparkles swirl around the warp core.

HEIDI (mid-20s, young and attractive, fresh-faced, wearing Starfleet engineering uniform with a wand holster on her belt) enters, carrying a PADD and looking concerned.

HEIDI
Clif, the transporter's acting up again. Someone tried to beam down and ended up with their molecules scattered across three decks. One guy's head is in the mess hall asking for coffee.

CLIF
Did you try Appareo Correctus?

HEIDI
I tried Appareo, but I forgot the Correctus part.

CLIF
(chuckling, moving closer)
That's why you're still in training, love.
(he touches her hand)
Here, let me show you again...

They stand close together, his hand over hers on her wand. Romantic tension.

HEIDI
You know we're not supposed to—

CLIF
I know. But some spells are worth the risk.

They're about to kiss when the door WHOOSHES open. CAPTAIN (50s, stern, classic Starfleet) enters with FIRST OFFICER SPOCK-TYPE (pointy ears, raised eyebrow).

CAPTAIN
(clearing throat loudly)
Am I... interrupting something?

Clif and Heidi jump apart.

CLIF
Just teaching her the finer points of molecular reconstitution, Captain. Very... hands-on training.

CAPTAIN
Right. And I'm teaching my yeoman the finer points of...
(pause)
Never mind. Clif, Heidi, we need to talk. Conference room. Now.

INT. USS ENTERPRISE - CONFERENCE ROOM - CONTINUOUS

The Captain sits at the head of the table. Clif and Heidi sit across from each other, looking guilty. The First Officer stands.

CAPTAIN
Starfleet regulations are clear. Fraternization between senior officers and subordinates is prohibited.

CLIF
With all due respect, Captain, I'm not technically an officer. I'm a... consultant.

FIRST OFFICER
A consultant who controls every critical system on this vessel. The shields, the warp drive, the transporters, the structural integrity field...

CAPTAIN
Exactly. Which is why this relationship is a problem. And let's be honest here—
(gestures at Clif)
Clif, you're old enough to be my father.
(gestures at Heidi)
And Heidi, you could be my daughter. This is... inappropriate.

CLIF
(standing, angry)
Inappropriate?! I'm the best damn wizard in the fleet! I've been keeping this ship together for 47 years! You want to talk about what's inappropriate? Starfleet pretending they have "advanced technology" when they know damn well the laws of physics make warp speed impossible! Every ship in this fleet runs on magic, and you know it!

HEIDI
(standing)
This is ridiculous! We're both adults!

FIRST OFFICER
(calmly, raising one eyebrow)
Captain, with respect, Lieutenant Commander Vaxor and Ensigns T'Pral and Martinez live together as a thruple on Deck 12. And there's the entire polygamist compound on Deck 27.

CAPTAIN
(waving dismissively)
That's different. They filed the proper paperwork.

FIRST OFFICER
(pause)
The needs of the many outweigh the needs of the few. Or the two.
(another pause)
Can Starfleet even afford to let you retire, Wizard High? Faster-than-light travel is scientifically impossible. We've known this for 200 years. Without wizards, we don't have warp drive. We don't have transporters. We don't have force fields. Without you, this ship is just an expensive metal tube floating in space.

CAPTAIN
(uncomfortable)
Look, we all know the truth. Starfleet will never crack warp technology. It's impossible. We need wizards. But that doesn't mean we can ignore regulations.
(decisive)
Fine. Clif, you can stay, but the relationship ends. Heidi, you can transfer to another ship, or you can resign.

HEIDI
(looking at Clif, then back at Captain)
I... I choose to resign.

CAPTAIN
Heidi, think about your career—

HEIDI
I have. And I choose him.

CLIF
(smiling)
Well, if she's resigning... then so am I.

CAPTAIN
(panicking)
Wait, what? No! Clif, you can't—

CLIF
(pulling out a small pouch)
Oh, but I can, Captain. I've got 47 years of unused vacation time, and I'm taking it all. Right now.

Clif throws FLU POWDER on the ground. Green flames erupt.

HEIDI
(grabbing Clif's hand)
Where are we going?

CLIF
Risa. I hear the beaches are lovely this time of year.

CAPTAIN
WAIT! WHO'S GOING TO RUN THE SHIP?!

CLIF
(grinning, winking at camera)
Not my problem anymore!
(to Heidi)
Ready, love?

HEIDI
Ready!

They step into the flames together and DISAPPEAR in a swirl of green smoke and sparkles.

FIRST OFFICER
Captain... the warp field is collapsing.

The ship SHUDDERS violently. Red alert klaxons blare.

CAPTAIN
(grabbing the table)
Does ANYONE on this ship know magic?! Anyone take a weekend course? Read a book?!

FIRST OFFICER
I am a Vulcan, Captain. We do not believe in magic. We believe in science. Which is precisely why we have no warp drive.

ENSIGN (O.S.)
(over intercom)
Captain! We're dropping out of warp! And the shields are down! And there's an asteroid field ahead!

CAPTAIN
(looking at camera, deadpan)
I should have just let them date.

Beat. One second pause.

The ship LURCHES. Everyone falls. Sparks fly.

FADE TO BLACK.

> END CARD <

White text on black background:

"Starfleet Wizarding Academy is now accepting applications.
Starting salary: 250,000 credits.
Relationship status: Negotiable."

FADE OUT.

THE END

